### Verifier: cancel-funded orders keep backing_tx_hash (VERIFY-1)

`exchange_verify.py` reported FAIL for every non-funded order keeping
`backing_tx_hash`, but the cancel path sets `funded_state='backing_expired'`
and keeps the hash on purpose — the monitor needs it non-NULL to build the
`order_refund` row and it is the audit link to the lock.

- `bcd72050a` — `--bridge-db` now feeds `order_refund` ref_id→status into the
  order-row check: `backing_expired`+hash passes when a pending or terminal
  refund row exists, reports INFO when the monitor DB is not provided, and
  still FAILs when no row exists (stranded lock) or the row is `failed`.
  Other funded-state rules unchanged. Docstring documents the hub AIT RPC
  port (`127.0.0.1:8202`, not the auth-gated 8201) and a `--settlement`
  example.


