### Verifier + monitor: settled-trade hash mirrored and cross-read (VERIFY-2)

`_set_status_and_mirror` persisted status+fields, then mirrored the stale
pre-update row, so the leg-seal sites passing `settle_ait_tx_hash`,
`settle_fee_tx_hash`, or `refund_tx_hash` as fields never reached the
`trade_state` post — settled trades kept NULL
`trades.settlement_ait_tx_hash` (D2 trade 7), which
`exchange_verify.py --settlement` then reported as a FAIL.

- `1cf09e4b1` — the mirror now posts `{**row, **fields}`: payload keys
  `eth_tx_hash`, `ait_tx_hash` (leg-1 settle or refund), and
  `fee_tx_hash`. `order_refund` rows still never mirror and the mirror
  stays best-effort.
- `1cf09e4b1` — `exchange_verify.py` with `--bridge-db` reads the
  settled trade-kind ledger row's `settle_ait_tx_hash`: a settled trade
  missing the column on the tape passes when the ledger carries it;
  no/unreadable monitor DB reports INFO 'settlement hash link unchecked'
  instead of a guess-FAIL. A missing `settlement_eth_tx_hash` stays a
  FAIL; no live DB was backfilled.

### Exchange: bridge routes resolve repo-relative imports (TEST-3b)

Second TEST-3 root cause, found on re-review: the bridge handlers
inserted literal `/opt/aitbc` paths into `sys.path`, so worktree and
scratch runs imported `bridge_monitor` from the live checkout — the
first storage fix was invisible to an isolated run (the earlier green
held only through `sys.modules` caching from earlier-collected test
modules). Verified: `TestRoutingTable` alone still failed at `423cddc9a`.

