### MSG-2d — stored-hash normalization fix (live vote proved the gap)

- The chain stores ``tx_hash`` ``0x``-prefixed while envelope
  ``target``/``parent`` fields are bare 64-hex (codec shape). Every
  derivation join compared the two forms literally, so votes, hide/pin,
  thread locks, reply ``parent_resolved`` and reputation silently
  matched nothing against production rows — caught live when the first
  MSG-2 vote sealed at block 49245 and read back as score 0. All suites
  passed because fixtures stored bare hashes on both sides.
- ``messaging_index`` now normalizes through ``_bare_hash``/``
  _tx_hash_bare`` (substr(-64) works for both stored forms); the affected
  joins are parent resolution, ``get_message`` (now accepts both forms),
  standing votes, score fields, hidden/pinned/after-lock views, locked
  subtree walks and reputation.
- Tests: new ``TestPrefixedStorage`` class (6) seeds ``0x``-prefixed
  ``tx_hash`` rows with bare env fields and re-proves parent resolution,
  both-form lookups, vote scoring, hide/pin, locked-subtree walks and
  reputation. The live vote at 0x782b…03cc reads correctly once deployed.

