### ETH-14: release gas estimation + receipt-gated completion + withdraw_admin recovery (2026-10-14)

Withdrawal `withdrawal_90ff8a73` was recorded `completed` on a broadcast
that reverted on-chain (gas limit 100,000 vs the ~207,391 a fresh-account
transfer needs post-Glamsterdam — Sepolia activated EIP-8037 state-gas on
2026-10-06). The broadcast echo was trusted as payment proof; the ETH-9
receipt machinery only ran on crash/resume paths, never the happy path.

- `bridge_withdraw_monitor.py`: `_release_eth_for_withdrawal` now leaves
  the row `releasing` after broadcast — `completed` is written only by
  the verified-outcome paths (`_resume_unfinished_releases`,
  `_resolve_release_failure`, the retry command). Gas is
  `eth_estimateGas(from, to, value)` × `ETH_WITHDRAW_GAS_MARGIN`
  (default 1.25), floored at 21,000, hard-capped by
  `ETH_WITHDRAW_GAS_MAX` (default 300,000); an estimate error or an
  over-cap result raises before signing. `ETH_WITHDRAW_GAS` survives only
  as an explicit override escape hatch (rejected outside (0, MAX]).
- `sell_escrow_monitor.py`: `_release_eth_for_lock` takes the same gas
  path and drops its post-broadcast `released` write — `_handle_inflight`
  verifies the receipt each poll and moves `releasing` → `released` →
  settle only on proof.
- `bridge_db.py`: additive `eth_withdrawals.retry_count` +
  `eth_withdrawal_release_attempts` (id, ait_tx_hash, eth_tx_hash,
  release_nonce, resolved_by, resolved_at, operator_note, outcome);
  resumable/pending status lists cover `releasing_retry` +
  `needs_review_release` — the parked retry status is deliberately NOT
  auto-resumed.
- `withdraw_admin.py` (new, `python -m wallet_app.bridge.withdraw_admin`
  on hub, in the unit env): `status`, `release-retry` (dry-run default;
  `--confirm --note` required to sign), `mark-review` (the refund
  fallback). `release-retry` refuses unless two independent Ethereum RPCs
  in the same run prove the recorded release reverted at depth + nonce
  consumed + receiver gained nothing in the failed block (or, for a
  retry that never sealed, hash absent + nonce still free), and the AIT
  `BRIDGE_WITHDRAW` leg is `confirmed`. The resend uses exactly the
  recorded `amount_eth`/`eth_address` at the current account nonce —
  never re-quoted — with intent (`releasing_retry` + nonce +
  deterministic hash + attempt row) persisted before broadcast. A
  verified `sent` completes the row; a proven failure parks it
  `needs_review_release` for the operator, never auto-refunds.
- `bridge_monitor.py`: dropped the dead `ETH_WITHDRAW_GAS` constant.
- Runbook: `docs/ops/withdraw-release-runbook.md`.
- Absence grace (follow-up): receipt verification now runs on the happy
  path, so a lagging RPC can report a just-broadcast release as absent.
  `_compose_release_outcome` treats an absence-only view (no receipt, no
  tx, nonce not pending) on a row whose release intent is younger than
  `ETH_RELEASE_ABSENCE_GRACE_SECONDS` (default `600`, measured from the
  row's `released_at` intent-write timestamp) as `unknown` — never a
  refund trigger. A status-0 receipt is `not_sent` at any age. Applies to
  `releasing`, `releasing_retry` and sell-escrow releases alike.

Tests: `test_bridge_withdraw_monitor.py` (broadcast-leaves-releasing,
estimate/margin/floor/cap/override, estimate-failure refund path,
releasing_retry park + sent, parked row not resumable),
`test_sell_escrow_monitor.py` (releasing → verified released on all
release tests), `test_bridge_db.py` (attempt record/retry_count/status
lists), `test_withdraw_admin.py` (dry-run purity, every refusal gate,
confirm→completed, revert→parked, single-use nonce reuse).

### ETH-15: keyed RPC URLs out of output, env precedence, log levels, runbook gaps (2026-10-14)

The ETH-14 recovery surfaced three hygiene gaps: `withdraw_admin` printed
the effective `ETH_RPC_URL` verbatim (a gateway URL carrying its API-key
path), httpx's INFO request lines logged the same URL into the
aitbc-wallet journal on every poll, and the admin's env-file loader
applied *first-wins* precedence where systemd `EnvironmentFile` — which
the unit actually uses — is *last-wins*.

- `wallet_app/bridge/url_redact.py` (new): `redact_url` /
  `redact_text` — `scheme://host[:port]` only; path, query, userinfo and
  fragments never reach stdout, the journal, or a stored field.
- `withdraw_admin.py`: every endpoint print (`_print_verdicts`, verdict
  dicts) stores only the redacted form; `_rpc_call`/`_ait_rpc_get` wrap
  httpx errors so exception text never carries the URL; stored attempt
  `outcome` text is redacted the same way. `_load_env_files` now collects
  file values first and applies them last-file-wins (systemd semantics)
  while an already-exported shell variable still wins — the documented
  operator override for picking the proof RPC pair. Proof refusals caused
  by a pruned endpoint now say "not archive-capable" instead of only the
  raw RPC error.
- `aitbc_logging.py`: `_HttpxStatusFilter` now drops sub-400 `HTTP
  Request:` lines entirely (they carried the full URL on every poll) and
  keeps 4xx/5xx at WARNING/ERROR with the URL rewritten to
  `scheme://host` — the error signal survives without the credential
  path; an unparseable `HTTP Request:` line is dropped rather than risk a
  URL. The httpx logger's level is untouched (a WARNING level would drop
  records *before* the filter could see them — silently killing the
  4xx/5xx signal); `httpcore` is set to WARNING. Shared setup, so wallet,
  exchange and bridge-monitor all inherit it.
- `aitbc/url_redact.py`: the redaction helpers live in the shared package
  so `aitbc_logging` can use them; `wallet_app/bridge/url_redact.py` is a
  re-export shim so bridge imports keep working.
- `bridge_withdraw_monitor.py` / `bridge_monitor.py`: `_eth_rpc`/`_rpc`
  wrap `raise_for_status`/transport errors so an HTTP failure's exception
  text (which embeds the request URL) is redacted before it reaches logs
  or error fields.
- Grace log level: `_compose_release_outcome_detail` returns the reason
  behind `unknown`; the withdraw resume pass logs an in-grace absence at
  INFO and the sell inflight check at WARNING (its row still parks
  `needs_review` — state transitions unchanged), while `unknown` after
  the grace window or for any non-absence reason stays ERROR.
- Runbook: documents sourcing the unit env before python starts (import-
  time `COORDINATOR_API_KEY`), the `&`-misparsing line in
  `blockchain-secrets.env`, the archive-endpoint requirement for the
  `block−1` balance proof (drpc/tenderly pair; publicnode is pruned,
  Infura flakes), and that `ETH_RPC_URL` also picks the broadcast
  endpoint on `--confirm`.

Tests: `test_withdraw_admin.py` (keyed URL never in stdout/stderr across
status/retry/mark-review incl. error paths, attempt outcome redaction,
env precedence), `test_bridge_withdraw_monitor.py` +
`test_sell_escrow_monitor.py` (in-grace log level vs. ERROR for real
unknowns), `test_aitbc_logging.py` (httpx/httpcore WARNING after
`configure_logging`).

### DEPS-2: venv-pinned pip in update.sh, copied-venv shebang repair, CLI version source (2026-10-14)

`update.sh`'s four bare `pip` sites now run `"$VENV_DIR/bin/python" -m
pip` with stderr visible, and a post-install assert proves pip resolves
inside the venv (`command -v`, `pip -V`, and the `bin/pip` shebang).
`setup-python-venv.sh --mode copy` repoints `bin/*` shebangs, the
