### CFG-1: `block_scoped_preregistered_transactions` defaults on (2026-10-14)

O-11 path A, decided by the operator 14 Oct. `f3260ea1f1` flips the
`ChainSettings.block_scoped_preregistered_transactions` default to True:
a node without `BLOCK_SCOPED_PREREGISTERED_TRANSACTIONS` can no longer
debit `account` at RPC time. With the flag unset, `/bridge` lock /
confirm / refund used to mutate `account` immediately; at
state-transition >= v14 that host's `aux_state_root` then differed from
the fleet's and its block would be refused (`sync_aux_root_rejected`).
The env override still works both ways — an explicit `false` keeps the
legacy path — and the fleet already carries the flag `=true` in
`/etc/aitbc/blockchain.env` on all five hosts (verified in the chain
units' `EnvironmentFile` list and in the running process env), so
running nodes see no behaviour change.

- `config.py`: field default `False` -> `True`.
- `bridge_transfer.py` / `poa.py`: the four `getattr` readers now fall
  back to `True` — a missing attribute resolves to the non-divergent
  path instead of silently restoring RPC-time debits.
- Tests: the 12 tests asserting the legacy RPC-time mutation path pin
  the flag off explicitly (6 files, each in its own patch style; no
  assertion weakened). `test_signature_skip_guard.py` gains the
  default-True and env-false-wins cases.
- Replay unaffected: the flag is read at RPC issuance and in the
  proposer mempool branch only; block import/apply never consults it.

The parked `dev/block-scoped-account` design (O-11 path B) still
describes where this goes next: a v15 rung that scopes the semantics to
the block version so no env flag decides consensus at all.

### ETH-11 phase 2: signed orders + node registration on the hub exchange (2026-10-14)

Phase 2 of `docs/design/eth8-exchange-page.md` (decisions DECIDED 14 Oct):
the hub exchange now accepts only **signed** order envelopes from
registered nodes, still entirely unfunded — placement moves no funds and
a match books a `trades` row but settles nothing (funded settlement is
phase 3 / ETH-16, gated on a clean ETH-2 live withdraw run).

- `db.py`: `node_registry` (seeded from the fleet wallet labels), the
  exchange-scoped `order_nonces` counter (explicitly not the chain
  nonce), and order columns `signature`/`envelope_hash`/`account_nonce`/
  `expiry_height`/`funded_state`/`cancelled_at`; `orders.status` gains
  `expired` via a table-rebuild migration preserving existing rows;
  `trades` gains `buyer_address`/`seller_address`/`fee_ait`. The design's
  `prepaid_eth` table was deliberately left out — it is phase-3 funding
  machinery with no phase-2 readers.
- `handlers/exchange.py`: `keccak256(canonical JSON)` envelope verify via
  the repo's `signature_recovery`/`crypto` primitives before any DB
  write; per-IP rate limit runs *before* the secp256k1 verify; nonce
  replay guard with byte-identical resubmit dedupe via
  `(user_address, envelope_hash)`; expiry bound to chain head; ±10%
  `EXCHANGE_PRICE_BAND_PCT` oracle band (feed stale → 503 like the quote
  endpoint); `EXCHANGE_MIN_ORDER_AIT`; per-node and book-wide open-order
  caps; cancel shares the placement `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` lock so
  cancel-vs-fill is a deterministic 409 for the loser; self-match never
  fills; watchlist flag for cancel-ratio abuse — flag-and-log only
  (never blocks), knobs `EXCHANGE_CANCEL_RATIO` (0.9),
  `EXCHANGE_WATCHLIST_MIN_PLACEMENTS` (10), `EXCHANGE_WATCHLIST_WINDOW_S`
  (86400); per-IP limits read `X-Real-IP` only from peers in
  `EXCHANGE_TRUSTED_PROXIES` (default `127.0.0.1,::1`); all phase-2 rows
  stay `funded_state='unfunded'`. Chart feeds `depth`/`ohlc`/`stats`
  (design §8, no phase marker) are deferred — read-only follow-up, no
  schema gap (trades/orders tick columns already cover them).
- Routes: `POST /api/orders` (signed), `POST /api/orders/<id>/cancel`,
  `POST /api/exchange/nodes/register`, `GET /api/exchange/nodes`,
  `GET /api/exchange/my-orders?addr=`. The signature is the credential —
  `X-Api-Key` stays only on the legacy unsigned path, which remains
  reachable by pinning `EXCHANGE_REQUIRE_SIGNED_ORDERS=0` (flag-off also
  404s the phase-2 routes).
- CLI: `aitbc exchange order place|cancel|my` and
  `aitbc exchange node register`, signing with the node's own wallet via
  `load_wallet_for_payment` (`--password-file`/`--password-stdin`; no
  secrets in argv/logs). `chain_id` resolves fail-closed through
  `resolve_chain_id` against the node's own RPC. MCP wrappers
  regenerated.
- Docs: exchange API documented by hand in `docs/apps/exchange/
  exchange.md` — the service is a `BaseHTTPRequestHandler`, excluded
  from generated OpenAPI by design; scenario 59 gains a phase-2
  Scenario D addendum.

