### ETH-13: sell-lock operator command — sell_admin (2026-10-14)

Builds the operator command the sell-escrow runbook flagged as a tool
gap, per `TOPOLOGY/2026-10-13-sell-lock-operator-command.md` (all six
open choices decided 14 Oct). `python -m wallet_app.bridge.sell_admin` —
hub-local root only, no new network surface, same
dry-run/`--confirm --note` contract and exit codes as `withdraw_admin`.

Verbs: `list`/`inspect` (read-only; the persisted intent is shown parsed
and the signed blob never prints), `confirm-swept <hash> --tx <sealed>`
(re-verifies the sealed outflow on-chain through the monitor's own
`_find_escrow_outflow` match rule — nonce + recipient + amount +
`payload.sell_ref` — then writes `settled`/`refunded`; no hash or
mismatch refuses), `requeue` (literal return to the intent's lane —
`released`/`refund_pending`; refuses while a sweep is in flight and when
the intent blob is unreadable), `write-off --reason` (terminal
`written_off`; refuses rows with a live send in flight), and `sweep-now`
(`queued_fee_*` only — one synchronous `_escrow_sweep` through the
monitor's own code path, same fee-float check and park outcome).

Ledger: `bridge_sell_locks` gains `resolved_by`/`resolved_at`/
`operator_note` via `init_db`'s `_add_column_if_not_exists` block — the
same mechanism `eth_withdrawals.retry_count` used — written on every
resolution; the row's `error` carries `operator:<verb>`.
`sell_escrow_monitor._expected_sweep` takes an explicit `lane` argument
so the admin can re-derive the expected outflow for a
`needs_review_sweep` row (whose status no longer names the lane).
`written_off` is terminal by omission from every status set, but a
written-off row that recorded a release tx still counts toward the daily
sell-release cap (`get_sell_eth_committed_since` filters on
`eth_tx_hash IS NOT NULL` for it — decided 14 Oct): the cap measures ETH
that left the wallet, and write-off bookkeeping does not undo a payment.
It stays fully out of the pending reserve — the reserve is for ETH not
yet paid.
`SELL_ESCROW_ENABLED` is not required — operator duties exist while the
feature stays dark; chain-touching verbs still need the sell config and
(for `sweep-now`) a loadable escrow key slot. Runbook
`docs/ops/sell-escrow-runbook.md` gained the real procedures.

Host gates (decided 14 Oct, enforced in code): the module refuses unless
euid 0 and `BLOCKCHAIN_MODE=hub` in the loaded env set, and refuses when
the bridge ledger file is absent — `init_db` can never create an empty
DB on the wrong host.

Commits: `c2b963f5b` (module + audit columns + cap rule + tests),
`4ada8732f` (host gates + settled/foreign-nonce/requeue-serialization
proofs). `docs/ops/sell-escrow-runbook.md` + this section land in the
