### OPS-6: exchange base default is the bare hub origin (2026-10-15)

`hub_exchange_url()` fell back to `hub_service_url("exchange")` —
`https://<hub>/exchange` — but hub's `/exchange/` prefix is deliberately
the wallet service's mount (exchange-deposit routes), so every node with
no explicit `exchange_service_url`/`HUB_EXCHANGE_URL` resolved the
signed-order surface to the wrong service and `aitbc exchange …` failed
without `--exchange-url`. The fallback is now the bare hub origin via a
new `hub_origin()` helper: the signed-order routes publish at their
natural `/api/*` paths (OPS-4 mounts them there). Explicit
`HUB_EXCHANGE_URL`/`EXCHANGE_SERVICE_URL`/config values still win —
nodes carrying the stale explicit `…/exchange` value are fixed by
OPS-5's per-node config step, not by this change.

Tests: bare-origin default, explicit-env precedence, and the updated
process-env assertion all pass in `test_hub_url_from_env.py`.

Commits: `b710f2574` (hub.py default + hub_origin + test + scenario doc).

### CLI-3: signed exchange ops resolve the envelope chain-id — /rpc-suffix probe fix + island-creds fallback + `config get <key>` (2026-10-15)

Every signed exchange op (`node register`, `node set-payout`,
`order place`, `order fund`, `order cancel`) resolved its envelope
chain_id by probing the node's RPC — `get_chain_id_from_health` tried
`<base>/rpc/proposer` then `<base>/health` expecting a ROOT base, while
`get_rpc_endpoint()` and node `blockchain_rpc_url` config hand it
`/rpc`-suffixed bases (`https://<hub>/rpc`). The probes hit
`/rpc/rpc/proposer` → 404 → `ChainIdLookupError` on every island host;
node2's first `set-payout` needed `--chain-id ait-hub.aitbc.bubuit.net`
to get through. The probe now strips one trailing `/rpc` before building
its client, so bare and suffixed bases resolve identically — this also
fixes the same latent failure in the `ai.py`, `agent_sdk.py`,
`gpu_resources.py` and `market/gpu.py` signing paths that feed
`resolve_chain_id` the same bases.

`_envelope_chain_id` additionally falls back to the island credentials'
`island_chain_id` (the required field written and validated at join)
when no node answers the probe — covers hosts whose only RPC endpoint
is unreachable. Explicit `--chain-id`/`CHAIN_ID` still win, the strict
probe still runs for hosts without credentials, and the fail-closed
abort is last — never a silent default.

`aitbc config get <key>` is now a real subcommand (it was an alias for
`config show` that ignored the key — OPS-5 had to read yaml via ssh
grep): prints the stored value of one key, exits nonzero when absent or
the file is missing, refuses the file-info denylist plus
passphrase/credential, and keeps bare `config get` as the show alias.
`--global` reads the global config file. MCP wrapper regenerated for the
new signature.

Commits: `e64b0b123` (probe normalization + creds fallback + tests),
`9e7daa873` (config get + tests + MCP regen).

### REPO-1: file-info denylist extension + env-names case + verify DB containment + OPS-4 nginx example (2026-10-15)

`system file-info --field`'s denylist only caught the literal `*_key`
spellings — `privatekey`, `api-key`, `pass_phrase` and friends all
slipped through. The check now normalises each candidate (strips `-`
and `_`, lowercases) and additionally refuses the exact names
privatekey, apikey, secretkey, passphrase, passwd, credential and
