  `PYTHON=<interpreter>`. Wired into all eight scripts with the defect
  class: check-mypy-changed.sh (was a hardcoded `venv/bin/python` —
  reported bogus type errors on new files), check-c901-ratchet.sh,
  check_deprecation_cleanup.sh, check-mcp-cli-drift.sh,
  check-cli-docs.sh, check-except-ratchet.sh, check-openapi-drift.sh,
  mypy-precommit.sh. Before/after in a venv-less worktree:
  check-mypy-changed failed a clean new file with "Type errors"; after,
  real mypy runs and passes it. Surfaced backlog, pre-existing and now
  finally visible: check-except-ratchet defaulted to python3
  *everywhere*, so its baseline drifted ~52 files while the gate ran an
  empty scan — `make except-ratchet`/`make ci` report it now.
- **MCP drift + generator format (row 36).** The drift check formats
  via `"$PYTHON" -m ruff` — the pinned venv ruff — instead of a
  version-skewed PATH ruff (0.16 vs 0.15 produced false 76-file drift);
  `generate_mcp_cli_tools.py` ruff-formats its own output so a plain
  regen is drift-clean in one step, and the printed `Run:` hint names
  the resolved interpreter.
- **Wallet suite env isolation (rows 54/55).**
  `apps/wallet/tests/conftest.py` module-top: a guard raises at
  collection if `aitbc.constants`/`wallet_app.settings`/`ApiKeyStorage`
  were already bound outside a test scratch (combined runs fail loudly
  instead of leaking — observed firing on a `tests/unit`-first run
  where constants had bound `CONFIG_DIR=/etc/aitbc`,
  `LOG_DIR=/var/log/aitbc`); ambient env Settings/DatabaseConfig parse
  is popped (DEBUG, APP_*/ENVIRONMENT/NODE_ENV, HOST/PORT, DATABASE_URL
  family, AITBC_HOME); AITBC_DATA_DIR/CONFIG_DIR/LOG_DIR and
  API_KEY_STORAGE_PATH are force-assigned to a `tempfile.mkdtemp`
  scratch cleaned at atexit. 303 wallet tests pass under `env -i` with
  DEBUG=release, `/nonexistent` marker paths and a postgres
  DATABASE_URL; nothing touches the markers.
- **Adapter contract + uvicorn pin (row 56).**
  `test_adapter_provides_handler_contract_attributes` asserts the real
  FastAPIRequestAdapter exposes every attribute handlers read off self
  (client_address, headers, path, command, request, rfile/wfile) —
  mutation-verified, deleting the client_address line fails it.
  `test_server_runs_uvicorn_without_proxy_headers` spies uvicorn.run in
  server.main() and pins `proxy_headers=False`, which TestClient
  bypasses.

`tests/unit/test_repo_python.py` covers all resolver branches including
a real linked worktree and a dangling venv symlink.

Commits: `af1b2adaa` (resolver + 8 hook scripts + generator format +
resolver tests), `d75f144d4` (wallet conftest isolation), `6d0d57b8e`
(exchange contract/pin tests).

