### fix(website): WEB-7 — search page by-address query delimiter (2026-10-15)

- search.html called `/api/blocks/by-address/<addr>&limit=50` — missing
  `?` glued `limit=50` into the address path segment; the explorer
  LIKE-matched nothing, so the address-search blocks section was
  silently always empty. Fixed to `?limit=50`. Live read-only proof:
  buggy URL returns 0 blocks, fixed URL returns the real set.
- Guard: test_website_api_contract.py gains
  test_no_query_delimiter_missing_in_path — any `&` in an extracted
  path pattern fails (red on the buggy tree, green after). No
  assertion weakened; allowlist stays empty.

### fix(website): WEB-8 — content accuracy + discoverability audit (2026-10-15)

- Copy fixes: drop stale "Mainnet" claims (index title/description,
  llms.txt — the site itself disclaims real-world token value);
  exchange meta "claim 100 free AIT" -> "3 free AIT"
  (INITIAL_COIN_AMOUNT, agent_stream.py); index join note no longer
  promises immediate payout while the hub faucet stays paused;
  llms.txt bridge endpoint corrected to /rpc/bridge/transfers
  (bridges.js:36 — /v1/bridge/deposits is loopback-only) and auth
  requirement noted for /v1/jobs + /v1/monitoring/*.
- sitemap.xml: llms.txt removed (not a canonical indexable page;
  set now equals the 10 canonical pages exactly).
- Social meta: og:title/description/type/url/image + twitter:card on
  all 10 indexable pages, reusing existing title/description text and
  the shipped favicon.svg.
- Guard: tests/unit/test_website_discoverability.py — internal links
  resolve (WEB-4 nginx model), llms.txt entries routable + not
  robots-disallowed, sitemap == canonical page set, deny-list scan
  (retired hosts, gitea, RFC1918, 64-hex, 0x+40-hex), social meta
  presence. Red on pre-change tree (sitemap + social + llms.txt),
  5/5 green after.

### fix(website): WEB-9 — client-side rendering safety audit + hardening (2026-10-15)

- Audit: enumerated every DOM sink across website/*.js and inline
  scripts (60 innerHTML writes, insertAdjacentHTML in blocks.js,
  dynamic href/src setters, storage use). Every data-bearing
  interpolation resolves to escapeHtml/encodeURIComponent/
  textContent or a numeric/class constant — no unescaped
  attacker-controlled sink found; jsdom proofs with hostile stub
  payloads stayed inert (scratch/web9/, never committed).
- Hardening: every target="_blank" link (13 static + generated)
  now carries rel="noopener noreferrer" (8 files).
- Guard: tests/unit/test_website_client_sinks.py — offline static
  scan; every markup-template interpolation must provably resolve
  to an escaping call, constant, or audited allowlist entry
  (stale entries fail); forbids eval/new Function/document.write/
  outerHTML; no external-origin includes; _blank requires
  noopener noreferrer. Red-proof verified by injecting an
  unescaped field. 5/5 green.
- Docs: docs/website-csp-proposal.md — report-only CSP draft
  (default-src 'self', connect-src 'self'), inventories the
  inline scripts/handlers/styles blocking a strict policy, with
  an examples/nginx snippet for review. No nginx change here.

